# WordPress PHP (packages)

- Edit shippable code under `packages/free/` or `packages/pro/` only.
- Free admin classes: namespace `CredentialVault\Admin\` under `packages/free/admin/`.
- Use `declare( strict_types=1 );`, WordPress coding standards, and `$wpdb->prepare()` for SQL.
- Escape on output (`esc_html`, `esc_attr`, `esc_url`), sanitize on input, verify nonces and capabilities in admin/AJAX/REST.
- Secrets: read/write only via `CredentialVault\Secrets_Bridge` or `credential_vault_get()` / `credential_vault_set()`; audit reads (`Query_Source` / `source` context); respect `credential_vault_user_can` and sudo gates. Test doubles use `pre_credential_vault_get` / `pre_credential_vault_set` and `CREDENTIAL_VAULT_TEST_MODE`, not a parallel store.
- New hook-based free modules: register from `CredentialVault\Extended_Features::register()`.
- Hook pro code on `credential_vault_loaded`; register new pro modules in `CredentialVaultPro\Plugin::register_pro_features()`.
- Text domains: `credvault` (free), `credential-vault-pro` (pro).
- After substantive changes, suggest `composer phpcs` on `packages/`.

Canonical bootstrap: `@packages/free/credential-vault.php`, `@packages/pro/credential-vault-pro.php`.
